<===> zero/README.md
Although zero is not a valid code point per spec, we pass it through exactly for
the identifier `\0` because it's used in browser hacks.

<===>
================================================================================
<===> zero/alone/input.scss
a {b: \0}

<===> zero/alone/output.css
a {
  b: \0 ;
}

<===>
================================================================================
<===> zero/start/input.scss
a {b: \0xyz}

<===> zero/start/output.css
@charset "UTF-8";
a {
  b: �xyz;
}

<===>
================================================================================
<===> zero/mid/input.scss
a {b: x\0y}

<===> zero/mid/output.css
@charset "UTF-8";
a {
  b: x�y;
}

<===>
================================================================================
<===> surrogate/leading/input.scss
a {b: \D800}

<===> surrogate/leading/output.css
@charset "UTF-8";
a {
  b: �;
}

<===>
================================================================================
<===> surrogate/trailing/input.scss
a {b: \DC00}

<===> surrogate/trailing/output.css
@charset "UTF-8";
a {
  b: �;
}

<===>
================================================================================
<===> too_high/input.scss
// Regression test for sass/dart-sass#1030.
a {b: \110000}

<===> too_high/output.css
@charset "UTF-8";
a {
  b: �;
}
